# Generate 3D > Hyper3D Rodin (direct) (ai/Hyper3D.h, #123): the tier picker, the key field and what is sent to whom;
# without a key Generate refuses before anything is sent; a studio policy that doesn't list "hyper3d" shows the
# Managed badge and refuses too. Nothing is generated (no key, no network).
run ui_look look=classic layout=classic        # written for the Classic look
drop ../../assets/demo/teddy-sketch.png
wait_for "Generate 3D" 5
click "Generate 3D/##service"
expect_text Hyper3D Rodin (direct) - paid, your key
click "Hyper3D Rodin (direct) - paid, your key"
wait 0.2
expect_text Off until you add your own key
expect_text Sends your image or description to Hyper3D (api.hyper3d.com)
expect_text billed to your Hyper3D account
shot generate-hyper3d-image

click "Generate 3D/Tier"
expect_text Gen-2.5 Extreme Low (fastest)
expect_text Gen-2.5 Extreme High (more credits)
shot generate-hyper3d-tiers
click "Gen-2.5 Medium"
wait 0.2
expect_text Gen-2.5 Medium

click "Generate 3D/Generate 3D model"
wait 0.5
expect_text Add your Hyper3D API key

click "Generate 3D/From text"
wait 0.2
expect_text Sends your image or description to Hyper3D
shot generate-hyper3d-text

run ui_policy json="{\"format\":\"sculptforge-policy\",\"version\":1,\"organization\":\"Acme Animation\",\"ai\":{\"enabled\":true,\"providers\":[\"fal\",\"huggingface\"]}}"
wait 0.2
expect_text doesn't allow this AI provider (hyper3d)
shot generate-hyper3d-managed
run ui_policy json=""
